cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FiabilityLab: A Jamovi Module for Reliability and Agreement Analysis"
message: >
  If you use FiabilityLab in your research,
  please cite the software using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Chacón Chacón"
    given-names: "Arquímedes De León"
    affiliation: "Universidad Católica Andrés Bello (UCAB), Caracas, Venezuela"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7014-7513"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ArchieJamDev/FiabilityLab"
license: "GPL-3.0-only"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-09"
abstract: >
  FiabilityLab is an open-source Jamovi module for evaluating measurement
  reliability and agreement: internal consistency, inter-rater agreement,
  confirmatory-factor-based (SEM) reliability, and measurement invariance
  across groups. It integrates a Library and Bibliography system to teach
  the theoretical foundations and assumptions behind each statistic.
keywords:
  - Jamovi
  - Statistics
  - Reliability
  - Inter-Rater Agreement
  - Measurement Invariance
  - Structural Equation Modeling
  - Research Methods
  - Open Science
language: en
